# The canon itself is meant to be committed. These are not:
# `seen` is this machine's ingest state and `draft-runs/` is the
# evidence from its model runs. Neither is an act.
seen
draft-runs/
# `config` names ONE machine's endpoint and model. `canon init` does not list
# it; canon's own repository does, so `canon draft` on a fresh clone says "no
# endpoint configured" instead of calling a port on this laptop (canon
# requirements doc, entry 17).
config
# `sources/` holds notes exported by scripts/canon-export-notes.py. This repo is
# PUBLIC and those notes were never in git; ignored until the operator decides
# whether they are published, so no grab-bag commit can publish them first.
sources/
